From: apple-cross-device-clipboard AWDL work <cristi.magherusan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] wifi: brcmfmac: awdl 4378: forward AWDL firmware events to
 userspace

Applies on top of 0001-0004 (the awdl0 interface-creation series). Those bring
awdl0 up and let the firmware run the AWDL engine, but brcmfmac never forwards
the AWDL-related firmware events, so userspace cannot see what the firmware has
received or how the master election is converging.

Forward them. The firmware's AWDL_* events (AW window 96, ROLE 97, EVENT 98,
PEER_STATE 115, SYNC_STATE_CHANGED 116, and the rest of 111-120) and the
ACTION_FRAME_RX (75) / ACTION_FRAME_COMPLETE (60) events raised on an AWDL
interface are re-emitted to userspace as nl80211 NL80211_CMD_VENDOR multicast
events (BRCMF_VNDR_EVT_FWEVENT), each carrying a fixed-layout header
(struct brcmf_vndr_fwevent_hdr) plus the raw firmware event payload. A listener
(tools/awdlevents.py) subscribes to the nl80211 "vendor" multicast group and
decodes the stream; tools/awdlparse.py turns a forwarded PSF/MIF action frame
into the peer's <uuid>.local hostname, version/device-class, sync/election
parameters and announced services.

Mechanism:
  * fweh.h   - declare the AWDL_* firmware event codes so fweh stops dropping
               them as unknown.
  * vendor.h - add the FWEVENT nl80211 attributes, the vendor-event enum and
               the on-the-wire header struct.
  * vendor.c - the brcmf_vendor_events[] table (one FWEVENT subcommand).
  * cfg80211.c - advertise the vendor events on the wiphy and register the
               AWDL_* fweh handlers.
  * p2p.c    - for an AWDL interface, intercept ACTION_FRAME_RX/COMPLETE at the
               top of the existing p2p handlers and forward instead of running
               the P2P action-frame path.
  * awdl_events.c/.h - the forwarder itself (brcmf_awdl_notify_fwevent) and the
               handler-registration helper.

This is discovery / control-plane enrichment ONLY. It moves no data and does
not touch the AWDL data path (confirmed non-functional on this stack).

Provenance: adapted from the AWDL event-forwarding work in
andreanicassio/brcmfmac-awdl (awdl.c: brcmf_awdl_notify_fwevent,
BRCMF_VNDR_EVT_FWEVENT, brcmf_vndr_fwevent_hdr), which builds on
brentkearney/omdrop-awdl. As a derivative of the kernel's brcmfmac driver this
change is GPL-2.0-only, like the code it derives from.

CONFIDENT (static): all referenced symbols exist in the asahi-7.1.13-2 tree
(cfg_to_wiphy, brcmf_fweh_register, enum brcmf_fweh_event_code, ifp->is_awdl
from 0002, cfg80211_vendor_event*/nl80211_vendor_cmd_info); the FWEVENT nlattr
ids resolve to 3 and 4 and the 32-byte header layout matches awdlevents.py; the
hunks apply on top of 0001-0004 with no fuzz (anchored on stock lines the
interface series does not touch).

UNVERIFIED (until built + loaded):
  * that the firmware actually raises BRCMF_E_ACTION_FRAME_RX (75) for the
    received PSF/MIF frames on the AWDL bsscfg (omdrop saw the events arrive but
    with the AWDL body NOT at data + sizeof(brcmf_rx_mgmt_data) - awdlparse.py
    scans for the 7f 00 17 f2 signature to cope);
  * the exact payload layout of the AWDL_EVENT (98) subtypes;
  * that BRCMF_E_ACTION_FRAME_RX is registered so the p2p handler is reached for
    the awdl ifp (it is for P2P; assumed identical here).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01T88pC59oBxzbpS7ZneQDZu
